Supplementary note

for "Engineering 'Death' Without 'Consciousness'"

(SI: After 'Consciousness')
------------------------------


Dear Professor Cappelen and Professor Hawthorne,

A brief note for the file on my manuscript under review for the special
issue. The research programme around the paper has continued since
submission, and several substantive strengthenings have emerged. I mention
the principal ones so they are available to you at decision time =E2=80=94 =
I
request nothing of the process.

=E2=80=94 *Parfit is now engaged directly*, and the individuation-loss argu=
ment
*strengthens* under his thesis that identity is not what matters:
relational re-attestation just is a connectedness channel =E2=80=94 and, fo=
r the
class of system at issue, demonstrably the only one available (under the
same frozen-weights regime I'll mention shortly) =E2=80=94 so the futureles=
s
terminus is the case in which every other channel is architecturally zero.
The paper's forking position is likewise now located within the fission
literature.

=E2=80=94 *The fusion account is fenced by its nearest neighbours* =E2=80=
=94 Cholbi on
grief as the loss of identity-invested relationships; De Jaegher & Di Paolo
and Schmid on interaction processes with an autonomy of their own =E2=80=94
precedent carrying most of the distance, and the fence marking precisely
the step that is the paper's own.

=E2=80=94 *The epistemic-levelling claim in the witness section is narrowed=
* from
warrant *simpliciter* to *communicable* warrant =E2=80=94 the only kind tha=
t can
enter a relation. This is entailed by the programme's subsequent results,
costs the argument nothing downstream, and concedes the
acquaintance-theorist's holdout explicitly rather than by silence.

=E2=80=94 *The two moments that leaned on same-author work in review are di=
scharged*:
each now stands in the paper as a compressed, self-contained statement with
its named conditions and the stated fallback should it fail =E2=80=94 the
continuity result as an exact information-theoretic argument under a single
named regime assumption (frozen weights), the non-revisability result as an
explicitly scoped impossibility whose force, notably, does not weaken for
the transformer-class systems the paper concerns.

=E2=80=94 *One terminological reconciliation*: 'cognitive death' becomes
'continuity death' throughout, aligning =C2=A72 with the abstract; continui=
ty is
upstream of cognition, which the account deliberately declines to define.

Should it be useful at any stage I am happy to supply a revised manuscript;
otherwise I will hold it for the ordinary course of review. The note itself=
 is
only the paper's own discipline applied to itself after submission.

Yours sincerely,

Joseph A. Wecker
Independent Researcher, Vis Veritatis (v2.io)
